#. EN: A moment that both know will end shortly takes this pressure out. Nobody has to deliver, nobody has to refuse. At the same time it engages the accelerator: the brain's reward system reacts particularly strongly to anticipation – to something that is in prospect but not yet fulfilled. And anyone with more responsive desire, meaning desire that only arises through closeness rather than being there spontaneously, gets small sparks spread through the day instead of a single cold start in the evening.
