#. Lektion im Kurs „13. Präsenz und erotisches Selbstmitgefühl“
#. EN: At twenty, a thought is often enough for an erection or wetness – but much is also over quickly, hectic and very focused on the genitals. Over the years this changes: many men need more direct touch for a full erection, many women find that the mucous membranes get drier and lubricant helps. This is often experienced as a loss.
#. EN:
#. EN: Why it works
#. EN: The change takes away sex's self-evidence – and that's exactly where the opportunity lies. Anyone who no longer functions automatically becomes slower, more attentive and enjoys more consciously. That is at the core of what this whole program practises: less performance, more perception.
#. EN: An erection that softens in between and returns through touch isn't failure. It takes the pace out and can lengthen your time together. Lubricant isn't a crutch, but a pleasure enhancer that turns friction into gliding.
#. EN: And much really does get better with the years: knowledge of your own body, less shame, more patience, more courage to voice wishes.
#. EN:
#. EN: The exercise
#. EN: Write down three things you can do better in bed today than ten or twenty years ago. Share them with your partner if you like, and ask each other.
#. EN: And put lubricant visibly on the bedside table – as a natural part of your lovemaking.
#. EN:
