#. Lektion im Kurs „25. Jeder Körper ist schön und sexy“
#. EN: Most of the bodies we see every day have been carefully selected, well lit and often edited. In advertising, on social media, in films and in porn, they show only a tiny slice of what people actually look like. Anyone who measures themselves against that can only lose. That's as true for women as it is for men, even though the ideals differ.
#. EN:
#. EN: Two ideals, one problem
#. EN: Women are often shown a slim, firm, smooth body: a flat belly, firm breasts, not a trace of cellulite, no hair except on the head. Men are often shown a tall, muscular body: broad shoulders, a six-pack, full hair, a big penis. Both ideals have one thing in common: very few people look like that, and even they often only with good lighting, the right pose and photo editing.
#. EN:
#. EN: How varied bodies really are
#. EN: Skin: it has pores, moles, freckles, spots, redness, scars and stretch marks, in women and men alike. The vast majority of women have cellulite, including very slim women.
#. EN: Hair: everyone grows body hair, sometimes thick, sometimes sparse, on the legs, armpits, belly, chest, back and around the genitals. Many men lose hair on their head over the years; that's very common and not a weakness.
#. EN: Belly and bottom: bellies are round, soft, and have folds or rolls when you sit. Bottoms are flat or round, firm or soft.
#. EN: Chest: breasts differ in size and shape, often even the two breasts of the same woman. Nipples are light or dark, large or small, flat or protruding. Men have a chest too, which can be flat, muscular or soft.
#. EN: Height and build: bodies are tall or short, narrow or broad, sturdy or slight. None of these shapes is naturally more attractive than another.
#. EN: Genitals: labia can be short or long, and the two sides are usually different. Penises are straight or curved. When soft they are sometimes smaller, sometimes larger, and that says little about how big they get when aroused. Testicles often hang at different heights.
#. EN: All of this is normal, not the exception.
#. EN:
#. EN: Why comparison hurts so much
#. EN: Our brain compares automatically. Seeing lots of edited images quietly shifts our inner yardstick. At some point your own, perfectly normal body starts to look like a mistake. So the problem isn't your body, it's the yardstick you measure it against.
#. EN: On top of that: anyone who struggles with how they look is often half in their head during sex. Instead of feeling, they watch themselves. That costs pleasure, which is exactly why it's worth changing this way of looking.
#. EN:
#. EN: The task
#. EN: For one week, notice which body images you come across: on your phone, in ads, in films. Each time, briefly ask yourself: is this real or staged? And what feeling does this image stir in me?
#. EN: If you like, also follow a few people or projects that show real, unedited bodies, of women and of men. Many find that this changes how they see themselves, too.
msgctxt "lesson:beauty_1#content"
msgid ""
"Die meisten Körper, die wir jeden Tag sehen, wurden sorgfältig ausgewählt, gut ausgeleuchtet und oft nachbearbeitet. In der Werbung, auf Social Media, in Filmen und in Pornos zeigen sie nur einen winzigen Ausschnitt davon, wie Menschen tatsächlich aussehen. Wer sich daran misst, kann eigentlich nur verlieren. Das gilt für Frauen genauso wie für Männer, auch wenn die Ideale unterschiedlich sind.\n"
